WEBVTT

00:00:02.581 --> 00:00:07.108
A smart bike at home should never be able to flood the service. Telo Ride now limits

00:00:07.108 --> 00:00:09.779
what one rider, or one connection, can send.

00:00:10.324 --> 00:00:16.544
Sixty rides an hour is the most one rider records. The sixty-first is refused with

00:00:16.544 --> 00:00:20.106
429, and Retry-After says how long to wait.

00:00:23.228 --> 00:00:28.332
It counts rides recorded, not requests: sending the same ride again still gets its

00:00:28.332 --> 00:00:30.624
first answer, and costs nothing.

00:00:36.133 --> 00:00:41.041
On the device, the ride waits. Results says the XP is on its way, and the outbox

00:00:41.041 --> 00:00:44.163
sends the ride again once the wait has passed.

00:00:49.038 --> 00:00:53.889
On the ride hub, two progress messages a second get through. The rest are dropped,

00:00:53.889 --> 00:00:57.739
and a client over the limit for ten seconds is disconnected.

00:01:01.942 --> 00:01:06.459
The app itself sends at most one every half second, so a rider never meets the

00:01:06.459 --> 00:01:07.106
limit.

00:01:12.266 --> 00:01:15.334
Results, waiting, from a phone to the full screen.

00:01:22.590 --> 00:01:27.193
Telo Ride, from the Telo family, turns a smart bike at home into a game.

00:01:27.538 --> 00:01:32.050
It pairs with the bike over Bluetooth, reads your power and sets resistance for

00:01:32.050 --> 00:01:33.721
every hill and interval.

00:01:34.066 --> 00:01:39.244
Two doors: Race (ride a map against your best-time ghost, bots or people) and

00:01:39.244 --> 00:01:44.692
Classes (ride along to a video, alone or with a group), fed by one progression of

00:01:44.692 --> 00:01:47.682
XP, rider levels, stars and map unlocks.

00:01:48.027 --> 00:01:50.520
A custom workout lives under Profile.
